WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.102
Jordan wants to help new students find
their way around

00:00:04.102 --> 00:00:08.025
school. She compares making an
illustrated guide to the whole

00:00:08.025 --> 00:00:11.947
school with testing one page about a
single hard-to-find room.

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:17.838
Relevance asks why the project matters.
Both ideas could help

00:00:17.838 --> 00:00:21.658
new students, and Jordan enjoys making
illustrations.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.848
Feasibility asks what Jordan could begin
with the time and

00:00:25.848 --> 00:00:29.717
resources she has. One page can start
with a sketch

00:00:29.717 --> 00:00:32.038
and feedback from a trusted adult.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:36.458
Scope asks how focused the idea is. A
guide to

00:00:36.458 --> 00:00:40.535
the entire school may be too big for the
first

00:00:40.535 --> 00:00:43.798
attempt. One room gives Jordan a clear
boundary.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:48.243
Jordan chooses the smaller guide. She
gives up wide coverage

00:00:48.243 --> 00:00:52.305
for now and gains a first draft she can
learn

00:00:52.305 --> 00:00:56.368
from. Use these lenses when you compare
your own directions.

